# SDK 58 is still in preview and ships react-native@0.88.0-rc.1, a PRERELEASE.
#
# Per node-semver, a prerelease version satisfies a range only if some
# comparator in that range shares its exact major.minor.patch AND carries a
# prerelease tag. So `0.88.0-rc.1` does not satisfy a plain range like
# `>=0.57`, even though it is numerically greater. npm reports this as e.g.
#
#   While resolving: @react-native-masked-view/masked-view@0.3.2
#   Found: react-native@0.88.0-rc.1
#   Could not resolve dependency:
#   peer react-native@">=0.57" from @react-native-masked-view/masked-view@0.3.2
#
# This affects every transitive package declaring a plain `react-native` peer
# range, so it is not fixable by bumping any single dependency. A plain
# `npm install` of the *official* SDK 58 preview template fails identically.
#
# Keep the SDK-pinned versions and relax peer resolution. Remove this file once
# SDK 58 ships a stable (non-prerelease) react-native, not merely when any one
# package widens its peer range.
legacy-peer-deps=true
